{"candidate_id":"figure-analysis:Figure3:f8cc7fa8fa0c2333","artifact_id":"Figure3","visual_type":"flowchart","description":"The figure illustrates the GEPA (Genetic-Pareto) optimization process as an iterative flowchart. It starts with initialization, enters a budget-controlled loop, selects candidates from a pool, applies one of two modification strategies, evaluates on a minibatch, and conditionally adds improved candidates back to the pool. Key components include a candidate pool visualized as a tree, a task-by-candidate scoring matrix, Pareto-based filtering, and the two core strategy modules: Reflective Prompt Mutation and System Aware Merge.","components":[{"name":"Initialization","role":"Starting point","visual_evidence":"A box labeled 'Initialize' at the top left initiates the process."},{"name":"Budget Loop Control","role":"Iteration controller","visual_evidence":"An oval labeled 'While Budget > 0' controls the main optimization loop."},{"name":"Candidate Pool P","role":"Repository of systems","visual_evidence":"A container labeled 'Candidate Pool P' holds a tree structure with nodes labeled P0, P1, P2, P3, P4."},{"name":"Scores Matrix","role":"Performance tracker","visual_evidence":"A grid labeled 'Scores Matrix' with rows for Task 1, Task 2, Task 3 and columns for candidates P0, P1, P4, P3, P2, showing checkmarks and X marks."},{"name":"Pareto-based Candidate Filtering","role":"Diversity-preserving selection","visual_evidence":"A section labeled 'Pareto-based Candidate Filtering' with a 'Filtered Pool (Pareto Frontier)' showing a subset of the candidate tree."},{"name":"Reflective Prompt Mutation","role":"Candidate modification strategy","visual_evidence":"A yellow box containing steps: 'Reflect and Propose New Prompt', 'Obtain text feedbacks using µf', 'Rollouts: Execute P2 on M', and a 'Minibatch M' cylinder."},{"name":"System Aware Merge","role":"Candidate combination strategy","visual_evidence":"A yellow box containing text about selecting prompts from candidates P2 or P3 and 'Sample 2 candidates to merge'."},{"name":"Evaluation Pipeline","role":"Performance validation","visual_evidence":"A flow from 'Sample 1 candidate for mutation' to 'Perform Minibatch Eval' producing Pnew, followed by a 'Performance improved?' decision diamond."},{"name":"Candidate Update","role":"Pool management","visual_evidence":"From the decision diamond, a 'Yes' path leads to 'Eval on all tasks + Add Pnew to Pool', while a 'No' path leads to 'Discard Pnew'."}],"relationships":[{"source_component":"Initialization","relation":"leads to","target_component":"Budget Loop Control"},{"source_component":"Budget Loop Control","relation":"controls selection from","target_component":"Candidate Pool P"},{"source_component":"Candidate Pool P","relation":"populates","target_component":"Scores Matrix"},{"source_component":"Scores Matrix","relation":"feeds into","target_component":"Pareto-based Candidate Filtering"},{"source_component":"Pareto-based Candidate Filtering","relation":"provides inputs to","target_component":"Reflective Prompt Mutation"},{"source_component":"Pareto-based Candidate Filtering","relation":"provides inputs to","target_component":"System Aware Merge"},{"source_component":"Reflective Prompt Mutation","relation":"produces candidate for","target_component":"Evaluation Pipeline"},{"source_component":"System Aware Merge","relation":"produces candidate for","target_component":"Evaluation Pipeline"},{"source_component":"Evaluation Pipeline","relation":"decision point leads to","target_component":"Candidate Update"},{"source_component":"Candidate Update","relation":"updates","target_component":"Candidate Pool P"}],"findings":["The flowchart depicts an iterative optimization loop that starts with an initialized candidate pool and continues until an evaluation budget is exhausted.","The process includes a 'Scores Matrix' that tracks performance of each candidate (P0-P4) across multiple tasks, indicated by checkmarks and X marks.","Pareto-based filtering is applied to the scores matrix to create a 'Filtered Pool (Pareto Frontier)' for candidate selection, which aims to ensure diversity.","Two distinct strategies for proposing new candidates are shown: 'Reflective Prompt Mutation' and 'System Aware Merge'.","Evaluation of new candidates (Pnew) is a two-stage process: first on a 'Minibatch M', and only if performance improves, a full evaluation is performed before adding to the pool.","The flowchart includes a decision node 'Performance improved?' that determines whether a new candidate is discarded or added to the pool after minibatch evaluation."],"citations":[{"section_id":"sec-3","path_id":"3","quote":"GEPA proposes a new candidate in every iteration by improving existing candidates using one of the two strategies (Reflective Prompt Mutation (Section 3) or System Aware Merge (Appendix D.1))"},{"section_id":"sec-3","path_id":"3","quote":"GEPA introduces Paretobased candidate sampling (Section 3.1), which filters and samples from the list of best candidates per task, ensuring sufficient diversity."},{"section_id":"sec-3","path_id":"3","quote":"GEPA begins with a candidate pool P containing only the base system, where each candidate is a concrete instantiation of ⟨Π, Θ f rozen ⟩ Φ"},{"section_id":"sec-3","path_id":"3","quote":"In each iteration, GEPA (i) selects promising candidates, (ii) proposes and evaluates a variant on a minibatch of tasks"}],"confidence":0.95,"provenance":{"image_sha256":"034b92eef1ddd19bff0ae4ef0a271e94eaf409b203dd0292dd2e251e5f47e1c5","context_sha256":"8419a00cb7cf79fbb2b5e772ee7641dda9c54ebb7d3b970d4c6a7cb0e5b6acde","route_id":"9router-anthropic","protocol":"anthropic_messages","requested_model":"minimax/MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","resolved_model":"mimo-v2.5-free","prompt_sha256":"997f902eb25e428191c73265b8a2ab169009cb7b36f38638f70fd25d6c77a34b","output_schema_sha256":"4ce0746fa9cd08cbb93bf629b39d8dd445baa44027c7505138168df1aa2a6d4b","input_tokens":6425,"output_tokens":2149,"latency_ms":40020},"authoritative":false,"import_eligible":false}